00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.578
We'll go through shot by shot,
talking about Easter eggs and WTF moments,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:49.449
starting with the episode title
Long Long Time, a reference to the Linda

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.550
Ronstadt song that

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.953
Frank and Bill played for each other,
which is all about surviving in general.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.588
Being alone. Human relationships.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.523
Being in love,

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.392
which was a big theme of the episode
and just of the Last of US

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.762
series in general,
trying to survive, allowing yourself

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:06.966
to be open to human relationships,
creating close bonds with each other.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.002
The opening
scene of the episode is of Joel and Ellie

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:12.439
right after the events of Episode two,
with Joel soothing his wounded hand nearby

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:15.642
in a stream and constructing
a pyramid out of rocks from the stream.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.878
The rock tower he's building
is just meant to be a memorial to Tess,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.748
like his way of eulogizing her,
remembering her because he's trying

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:25.085
to push past all these negative emotions,
all this sadness inside him.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.486
That's the big thing with his character.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.189
Like he doesn't want to have anything
to do with dealing with his feelings.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.992
There'll be no therapy in this episode
or future episodes any time soon.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:33.960
That's one of the big differences

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.396
with Ellie's character,
is that she wants to open up.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.064
She wants to talk about
all of these really hard

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.999
things, these traumatic things
that happen to them.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.168
But Joel doesn't want to deal
with any of that stuff right now.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.803
At least he's going to tamp down

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:47.073
on all those terrible negative feelings
inside me and continue on.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:50.610
He's just about sheer survival right
now, like he's in pure survival mode,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.913
going to tamp down all those terrible
negative emotions inside me.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.183
The part that they cut from the game
here is at the end of episode two,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.153
they have to continue escaping
the rest of the way out of Boston.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.489
In the game,
they use the abandoned subway terminals

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.924
until they get to the woods
outside of Lincoln,

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.127
which is where they're headed
to where Bill lives.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:10.497
The fact that Joel gave her his jacket
here to stay warm is also meant to be

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:13.500
a sign that he's slowly
treating her in a more caring way,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.502
like he's
being a little bit more thoughtful,

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.837
even though he's still trying
to push her away.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:21.141
As you see at the end of the episode, it's
not because he totally hates Ellie

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.977
or he blames her for Tess's death
or anything like that.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.480
It's just that he's afraid to get close
to other people because ultimately

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.451
he feels like he's going to lose them
and will just make him feel even worse.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.920
He doesn't want to hit rock bottom
emotionally again,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.989
like he actually genuinely
cared about Tess,

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.726
and it hurt badly to lose her
after losing his daughter.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.461
So he doesn't want to go
through the pain of that again.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:44.664
And that's why he doesn't want
to get close to Ellie, at least right now.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.966
But it all goes back to the
theme of the episode that Linda

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:51.204
Ronstadt song and the whole idea of Bill's
arc in the series

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:54.440
and how he got close to Frank
and how it ultimately fulfilled him.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.611
He was happy to go out the way that he did
because Frank had enriched his life

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.412
so much.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.247
So a lot of Bill's
storyline in the episode,

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.682
especially the message that he leaves for

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.585
him, is meant to inspire Joel
to get closer to Ellie.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.054
Ultimately,
it'll be worth it for better and worse.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.656
It's about a lot of these
early parts of the series.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.725
You see Ellie's influence on him,
like she's relentlessly positive

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.628
in the face of all this terrible stuff
that's happening to them.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.031
Just a lot of her
enjoying things in the moment.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:21.000
A lot of the first that she has,
like seeing the forest for the first time,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.770
like she's never been camping,
never been outside the quarantine zones,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.471
she's never been in a car before.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.840
So the whole idea
is that you see little moments like this

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.642
throughout the episode,
throughout the series,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.610
the first couple of episodes

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.080
where Joel slowly starts to act
a little bit more like a dad with her.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.082
If you zoom in enhanced on her backpack
here, too,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.952
you notice that she has her monster
keychain from the games.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.719
Little Easter Egg.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.854
I don't think that Neil Druckmann
has ever explained

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.091
where the actual monster
keychain came from or what inspired it.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.795
It looks like it's either based on Pixar's
Monsters Inc, like Microsoft's Psyche

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.630
or the Ugly Dolls line of toys.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.198
We might learn how she actually got it

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:55.969
in the flashbacks in her origin story
when they tell those in future episodes.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.570
The reason
why she doesn't have the backpack

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.973
from the games yet
like this is a slightly different backpack

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.842
is because she doesn't get that one
until much later in the first game.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:06.212
So we might also see her
get that backpack in a future episode

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.213
because for the most part,

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.382
like the clothes that she's wearing,
the clothes that Joel is wearing,

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:12.619
pretty much everybody else, for
the most part, are right out of the game.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.854
They're meant to be fairly accurate
costumes.

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:17.957
Later in the episode, Ellie
also gets another one of her video game.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:18.825
T shirts.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.059
Even during episode two.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:24.397
The lighter that Tess used to sacrifice
herself is right out of the games.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:27.600
Neil Druckmann said that the costume
department in the props department

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.835
paid special attention to that.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:32.138
They were always asked how to make things
look more like they did in the game.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.041
A lot of their dialog here
is also taken directly out of the game.

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:39.178
Only rabbit in the woods.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:39.812
What?

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.082
Nothing. That's just.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.550
I've never seen anything like this.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.386
That's all you need in the woods?

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:49.022
Yeah. Never walked in the woods.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.990
It's kind of cool.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.760
The reason why Joel is taking them to
Bill's is because he thinks

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.861
that they can get a car there

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.930
that will take them the rest of the way
to Wyoming, to Jonesboro, either

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.733
because of the timing of the episode
when a bunch of the big events

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:01.501
wind up happening.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.269
At this point,
when he's taking them there,

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:06.105
he still thinks that Bill and Frank
are still alive.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.042
The way they timed this,
the way the countdown works on the radio,

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.576
the warning message that goes off,

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.646
it sounds like they died
right before the events of episode one.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.782
But as they start
hiking the rest of the way,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:19.352
Joel starts to explain to her
that the real danger here isn't so much

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.155
the infected, it's
actually the Raiders, the real people.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:22.922
And that's a big thing

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.458
throughout the entire Last of US
series through the games.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:29.495
The idea that people are just as bad
as the fungus, we will continue

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:33.766
to meet very terrible, very bad people
as we go along through the series.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.936
In fact, Troy Baker, who did the voice of
Joel in the games, is actually

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.939
playing one of the antagonistic characters
later in the series.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.141
No spoilers
about what's going on with their group

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.143
because we will see them
in a future episode.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.680
But this is Troy Baker from the Games
they also use a lot of Bill and Frank's

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.051
flashbacks to show you that sometimes
humans can be just as bad as the infected.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:55.154
Like when Ellie finds the bodies
next to the downed airplane,

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:57.790
he explains that all the people
were killed by the military

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.860
not because they were infected,
but because they didn't have room for them

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.061
in the quarantine zones.

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.563
And it was very much shoot first,

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.865
ask questions later,
which is another reference to the

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:09.635
death of his daughter, like she died
even though she wasn't infected.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:12.438
Bill makes a lot of references
to the government during the episode too.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.707
Like you shouldn't trust the government.
They're all terrible.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.242
Turns out he was right.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:19.912
Joel starts referencing people and things
that they'll reveal in future flashbacks,

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.449
like how he got the scar, who Frank is
when they're looking for supplies

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.351
in the convenience store
that Joel keeps stash.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.687
Ellie finds the Mortal Kombat
two arcade machine.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:30.423
It's a reference to an in-game Easter egg
for Mortal Kombat.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.659
Two had a poster of it on her bed
at the beginning of the game.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.093
The friend

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:37.330
she mentions who was really into
it is Riley, who she's referenced

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.899
a couple of times in the series
so far, played by Storm Reed.

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:42.001
We'll see her in future flashbacks.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:42.969
All of her story

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:46.906
takes place before Ellie met Joel,
so it'll all be dealt with in flashbacks.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:50.243
While she's exploring the story,
she finds the trapped remains of either

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:53.479
the former owner or a fellow survivor
who had been infected and trapped there

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.814
while the ceiling had collapsed.

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:56.549
He's meant to be in the Shamblers state,

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.117
which is what they turn into
a little while

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.420
after the initial stage,
which are runners.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.522
The collapse seemed like
it happened a long time ago, but

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:06.292
maybe he just didn't turn fast enough
because the body couldn't find enough fuel

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:10.096
that the fungus didn't have enough fuel
to evolve him into the next day.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:13.199
This whole scene is about her
taking her anger out on it, showing

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:14.100
that she's not afraid,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.470
mostly to reassure herself,
but also as a cathartic way to deal with

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.072
all the really messed up stuff
that's happened to her

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.707
in all the even more messed up stuff

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.976
that happened in the flashbacks
that we haven't seen yet.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:27.213
So it's less of her trying to do something
good, putting it out of its misery

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.816
than it was about her finding catharsis
through it.

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:32.852
Also to show you that
she's not quite as helpless as she seems,

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:33.820
which also dovetails

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.823
with the idea that she keeps asking Joel
for a gun throughout the episode

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:40.326
until she finally finds Bill's gun
at the end of the episode.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:42.528
That'll probably come in handy
pretty soon.

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:45.097
The crash plane isn't meant to be
the same one from episode one,

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:46.766
because that was happening
way down in Austin.

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.301
But it is a callback to that.

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:52.004
The whole idea is Joel's explaining
what happened is that during the chaos,

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:52.839
people started turning

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:57.176
while these planes were mid-air, causing
most of them to crash all over the world.

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:57.944
Joel, saying that

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:01.681
he knows how to fly is another reference
to his history in the military.

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:05.318
They also have an Easter egg for Sully's
plane from Uncharted in the Last of US

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.619
games because Naughty Dog,

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:10.056
who make the Last of US
games, also made the Uncharted games.

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:12.825
Joel explains the origin of the cordyceps
fungus to Ellie,

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.261
which we saw during the flashbacks
in episode two.

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:17.797
And his explanation,
which he's just making an educated

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:19.232
guess about, is totally correct.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:22.668
The cordyceps was a common fungus
that mutated and infected

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.771
the flower made in the world's
largest flower factory in Jakarta.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:29.675
It was distributed all over the world,
winding up in people's food products,

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:30.510
Even though there was that

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.745
one person that the military lost
track of, like, well,

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.380
we don't know where
that one person went to.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.184
And they theoretically went around biting
people and the fungus spread that way.

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:41.287
It spread across the world
even faster because of the flour.

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:43.856
The big takeaway
here is the switch to eating more rice

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:45.925
instead of so much bread
and flour products.

00:08:45.925 --> 00:08:47.159
This episode, sponsored

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:51.330
by Rice, also confirms
the pancake flour theory from episode one.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.300
The reason why he, his brother
and his daughter didn't turn like

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:54.901
everyone else

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:57.503
is because they were out of pancake flour
that day,

00:08:57.503 --> 00:09:00.006
whereas their neighbors had the biscuits,
the cookies.

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:01.841
He goes on to recall
everything that happened

00:09:01.841 --> 00:09:05.177
that night in 2003
that we saw part of during episode one.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.179
At this point, he's
not speculating anymore because he's

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:11.083
speaking from experience like he's
recounting things as they happened to him.

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:13.553
And even though we're still kind of
dealing with a global pandemic

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:16.522
in real life right now, everything
that's happening in the episode

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:19.225
isn't meant to be a reference to that,
even if it feels like it.

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:22.395
All the stuff with the fungus spreading
and all that craziness was written

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:23.963
more than ten years ago.

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:26.966
It is a very dark coincidence
that we're going through something similar

00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:28.501
in real life right now.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:33.105
Also, in the games, the present day
is meant to be 2033, not 2023.

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:34.574
After Ellie learns about all the extra

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:37.810
terrible things that Federer did,
killing all the regular people in addition

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:42.014
to the infected, they pin it on the dead
bodies of the mother and her baby,

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:47.720
flashing back to September 30th, 2003,
to show you Bill's origin story in Franks

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:51.223
and this entire part of the episode, all
these flashbacks are not from the game.

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:53.192
This is a big change,
but I actually think it's

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:56.162
a really good change in it actually bodes
well for future seasons.

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:58.531
Like a lot of people have problems
with The Last of US too.

00:09:58.531 --> 00:09:59.799
Video game story.

00:09:59.799 --> 00:10:02.501
This means when they eventually adapt
that stuff in future seasons,

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:04.604
they can change it for the better.

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:07.306
The whole idea in the video games
is they find a version of Bill,

00:10:07.306 --> 00:10:10.376
but it's like a much darker version
of the character long after

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:13.379
Frank has died
and is driven him to a very dark place.

00:10:13.379 --> 00:10:16.349
It's a much more depressing
take on this whole encounter

00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:17.783
that they have in the episode,
in the message

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:20.820
that Bill gives them in the TV
version of the episode.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.789
In the game, Bill was meant to be a darker
mirror for what could

00:10:23.789 --> 00:10:27.526
potentially happen to Joel
if he continued to push people away.

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.462
But they show you
how Bill was a survivalist,

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.197
and that's part of the reason
why he was able

00:10:31.197 --> 00:10:33.466
to survive
the initial outbreak of the fungus,

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:36.135
because his house was essentially
constructed like a fortress.

00:10:36.168 --> 00:10:36.702
He'd already

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:40.406
all kinds of defensive measures, set up
all kinds of weapons, like his gear,

00:10:40.406 --> 00:10:44.310
his whole shelter here created
long before the fungus actually happened.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.079
