00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:17.643
Ellie finds Bill's handgun
finally getting a gun

00:21:17.643 --> 00:21:19.244
that she'd been asking
for this whole time.

00:21:19.244 --> 00:21:21.880
I think this is meant to be
the one that he always carried on his hip.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.015
Pretty safe to assume

00:21:23.015 --> 00:21:26.084
that gun is going to come in handy
eventually when they take off.

00:21:26.084 --> 00:21:29.855
Joel, getting the seatbelt for her is him
also being kind of like a dad.

00:21:29.855 --> 00:21:33.458
A lot of dad energy from Joel at the end
of the episode, going on a road trip.

00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:34.426
Got to play a mix tape.

00:21:34.426 --> 00:21:37.663
She finds the mix tape
that Frank made for Bill in the song.

00:21:37.663 --> 00:21:41.433
Playing on it is the Linda Ronstadt song
like that was meant to be Bill

00:21:41.433 --> 00:21:42.467
and Frank's song.

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:45.304
That's why he put it on the mix
tape. Like, This is our special song.

00:21:45.304 --> 00:21:48.974
The window that the camera ends on
is the bedroom window where they died,

00:21:48.974 --> 00:21:50.809
because he said in the letter
that he left the window

00:21:50.809 --> 00:21:52.878
open to keep the house from sticking up.

00:21:52.878 --> 00:21:54.913
And like I said,
as they played the song over

00:21:54.913 --> 00:21:56.515
the end of the episode,
as they drive away,

00:21:56.515 --> 00:21:58.483
the lyrics of the song are also meant
to be a metaphor

00:21:58.483 --> 00:22:00.218
for the future of John Ellie's
relationship.

00:22:00.218 --> 00:22:01.987
Finding someone else to care about

00:22:01.987 --> 00:22:04.556
is probably going to go down
as one of the best episodes of the series.

00:22:04.556 --> 00:22:07.292
Like I said, so it'll be interesting
to see if they can top this later

00:22:07.292 --> 00:22:08.193
this season.

